DISTRIBUTION SHAPE

Placement Gate is self-contained. Its only runtime dependency is pydantic:

    git clone https://github.com/Wyrd-Flux/placement-gate
    python -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install .

The placement primitives -- hardware observation, model profile, placement
planning and admission, the Ollama adapter, the ledger, and the verified load
seam -- are files under pgate_demo/placement/. Nothing else is needed. No
environment variables, no source-tree bindings, no private corpus, no cross-
repository dependency.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

HISTORY: THIS CODE WAS ONCE A SEPARATE PACKAGE

The placement primitives were extracted from an internal source repository for
the public release, published first as a separate Apache-2.0 package
(Wyrd-Flux/wyrd-placement-core), and then folded into this repository when it
became clear that package had exactly one consumer.

That repository was archived, not deleted. Its commit history, its own
PROVENANCE.md, and the AST comparison proving the placement seam is unchanged all
remain readable. This repository's git history was not rewritten either: the
adapter-only release and the separate-core release are both still present.

For code moved into pgate_demo/placement/, docs/PROVENANCE.md records:

  * the original internal source path for each file
  * the source SHA-256 for each file
  * the public core commit the code passed through
  * the extraction changes, including the one schema subtraction
  * the AST comparison proving the seam is byte-equivalent in logic
  * authorship counts and the absence of any upstream license file

